  intro: 'Octave Electronics was a small New York company. Its CAT was a compact, affordable duophonic synth: two oscillators with several waveforms each, playing two notes at once through one filter. It was often compared with the ARP Odyssey. Octave revised it several times, and Behringer’s CAT follows the last revision, the CAT SRM II.',
